the saints row series is back and  looking to reinvent itself instead of  picking up where part 4 left off this  new entry is taking you back to the  beginning with an all-new cast of  characters causing mayhem in a brand new  city here's everything you need to know  about saints row  saints row is all about creating your  own criminal empire if you think that  sounds familiar you're right because  it's not too far off from the goal of  the original game however instead of  spreading your influence across  stillwater the new saints row is set in  the fictional city of santo eliso this  huge and vibrant sandbox is located in  the southwest united states and seems to  combine the vibes of life locations like  las vegas and albuquerque at the start  of the reboot you're a member of a  private military corporation and all you  want to do is make enough money to cover  your half of the rent however when  climbing the corporate ladder doesn't  quite work out you turn to climbing the  criminal ladder instead are we gonna  make rent we'll make rent we just gotta  be a little more creative  last time we got creative i got stabbed  three times hey it would have been four  times if nina and i hadn't shown up your  roommates slash literal partners in  crime consists of the business  mastermind eli who cares more about  making the money than how the money is  made the getaway driver nina who is a  member of the muscle car and exercise  obsessed los panteros as well as the  people pleaser kevin who is a member of  the anarchist nightclub owners known as  the idols with this opportunity to start  over series developer volition wanted to  create criminals that were more  relatable and one way of doing that is  to show them starting from nothing  another way is to include characters  that are struggling to pay back student  loans because what's more relatable than  that the team also thought it was  critical to introduce new characters due  to some major changes in saints row 4  which i won't spoil here but if you know  you know  [Music]  like previous games in the series saints  row features familiar third-person  shooter gameplay in order to expand your  criminal empire you'll be engaging in a  bunch of different activities including  main quests side quests as well as a new  activity called criminal ventures  another new addition to the saints row  formula comes in the form of more  options for vehicle combat from side  swiping your enemies to hopping on top  of the car and firing back as you surf  on it there are multiple new ways to  take on your foes while moving there's  also the addition of a wingsuit so you  can fly around the city for fun or eject  yourself from the car open your wingsuit  and escape in style and there's also  your typical video game stuff like  completing missions earns you experience  points that play into a leveling system  leveling up takes you along a linear  progression path earning either new  equippable skills or earning you passive  upgrades like boost to your overall  health the skills are the cool part as  you can assign them to a certain button  and use them in the heat of battle and  saints row also includes a variety of  gameplay challenges you can complete  while you're doing other things with  objectives like driving the oncoming  traffic lane for a certain amount of  time or shooting a certain number of  enemies in the head with a specific kind  of weapon completing these challenges  unlocks perks you can equip to your  character to further customize their  abilities slots to equip more perks  unlock as you spend the money you earn  in the game creating a whole system that  incentivizes you to mess around with  saints row and engage with its various  aspects while adding new ways to deck  out your character according to your  playstyle with the game's new in-depth  character creator you'll be able to  change nearly everything about your boss  of course there are tons of clothing  options as well as the return of layered  clothing but in saints row you'll also  be able to customize your skin down to  details like texture glossiness color  veins scars tans body hair etc you can  also change the features of your entire  face and make it asymmetrical a new  addition to the series for a very  memorable look and the deep  customization doesn't stop at your  character's body there are also a lot of  ways to personalize the game's vehicles  and weapons as well  like previous games in the series saints  row will feature drop in dropout  cooperative online multiplayer allowing  for you and one other friend to team up  and play together completing missions  while in co-op will transfer over to  your own save so you won't waste time or  lose your boss's character progression  by playing in someone else's game so if  you've just started but you play a late  game mission with a buddy the game will  remember that and won't force you to  play that mission again once you reach  it in your own save  volition plans on releasing three  post-launch expansions for saints row  all of which will be included in the  game's expansion pass they haven't  revealed details about the packs just  yet but we're sure they're filled with  mayhem make sure to subscribe to  gamespot so you can get the details when  they're announced  [Music]  similar to the rest of the series saints  row is being developed by volition and  published by deep silver in an interview  chief creative officer jim boon  mentioned the team abolition used a  handful of action films as reference for  the reboot films like baby driver for  its vehicular movement hobbs and shaw  for its extravagance and john wick for  its stylized combat jim added that  today's social climate has outgrown the  tone of prior saints row games aka  moving away from sex toys as weapons was  a bit of a needed change  saints row will be released on ps4 ps5  xbox series xns xbox one and pc via the  epic game store  saints row was scheduled to launch on  august 23 2022 the game was originally  set to release on february 25th before  being delayed so that the team could do  a little bit more fine-tuning it's  available for pre-order both through the  game's official website and select  online retailers there are three  physical additions to the game standard  for 60 dollars chrono customs for sixty  dollars and notorious for ninety dollars  there are also three digital editions of  the game standard for sixty dollars gold  for ninety and platinum for one hundred  all six editions have the idols anarchy  pack as a pre-order bonus but you'll  also get the saints criminal customs  pack for pre-ordering the criminal  customs notorious gold or platinum  editions the physical criminal customs  edition adds the saints criminal customs  pack so it's basically just an addition  designed to give you an extra bonus for  pre-ordering the game so since it costs  the same as the standard edition you  might as well nab the criminal customs  edition if you're planning on  pre-ordering finally the notorious  edition adds the expansion pass and  comes with physical collectibles  including a steelbook case like the  physical version the digital version of  the standard edition only comes with the  base game the gold edition adds the los  panteros american muscle bundle and the  expansion pass while the platinum  edition includes all of that plus a  digital copy of saints row the third  remastered  so let's recap the new saints row  features new characters a new city  deeper customization new vehicle combat  a wingsuit and loads of ways to cause  chaos as you rise to the top of the  criminal food chain that's everything  you need to know about saints row hit  the comment section and let us know if  you plan on playing the game when it  releases and if you've pre-ordered which  one did you get make sure to subscribe  to gamespot so you don't miss out on any  new updates as well as our saints row  review when it's available you can find  me on social media at devonta chisholm  thanks for watching  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

